---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { ARCHIVE_REPO_URL, WEBSITE_REPO_URL, SUBREDDIT_URL } from '../lib/config.mjs';
---
<Base title="About" section="about" description="What the Intelligence Scaling Archive is and how it works.">
  <div class="prose">
    <h1>About the archive</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      The <a href={SUBREDDIT_URL} rel="noopener">r/IntelligenceScaling</a> (Smart Character Debates) community writes a
      lot of long-form work: character analyses, feat lists, debunks and original stories, some of them hundreds of
      pages long. Most of it lives in Google Docs that their owners can delete at any time, and 118 of the links in
      the community libraries were already gone when this archive started.
    </p>

    <h2>What's here</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Docs</strong>: analyses of characters, feats, series and matchups.</li>
      <li><strong>Stories</strong>: fan fiction and original stories.</li>
      <li><strong>Misc</strong> (coming later): tier lists, community boards and notable posts.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Each entry keeps its title, author (when known), series, characters, tags and its original links. A PDF and DOCX
      copy of each doc is saved, and a plain-text copy makes the full text searchable.
    </p>

    <h2>How it's built</h2>
    <p>
      Both parts are public on GitHub. The <a href={ARCHIVE_REPO_URL} rel="noopener">archive repository</a> holds the
      metadata and plain text of every entry, and the <a href={WEBSITE_REPO_URL} rel="noopener">website repository</a>
      builds this site from it. The site is plain static files, with no accounts or ads. It counts visits with
      Cloudflare Web Analytics, which sets no cookies and doesn't follow you to other sites, so we can see which pages
      people use.
    </p>

    <h2 id="adding">Adding something</h2>
    <p>
      Know a doc or story that should be here? A submission form is coming. Until then, open an issue on the
      <a href={`${ARCHIVE_REPO_URL}/issues`} rel="noopener">archive repository</a> with the link.
    </p>

    <h2>Credit and removal</h2>
    <p>
      Everything archived here is © its author. Authors can <a href="/removal/">ask for removal or a credit change</a>
      at any time. The people who built the community libraries this started from are thanked on the
      <a href="/acknowledgments/">acknowledgments</a> page.
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>
